$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=} \dfrac{420 \text{ kcal}}{1\text{ h}}  \cdot\dfrac{1\text{ h}}{60\text{ min}}\cdot\dfrac{1000\text{ cal}}{1\text{ kcal}}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{420\cdot 1 \cdot 1000 \cdot \cancel{\text{kcal}}\cdot\cancel{\text{h}} \cdot \text{cal}}{1\cdot 60 \cdot 1\cdot\cancel{\text{h}}\cdot \text{min} \cdot \cancel{\text{kcal}} }
\\\\
&=\dfrac{420{,}000}{60}\,\dfrac{\text{cal}}{\text{min}}
\\\\
&=7000\,\dfrac{\text{cal}}{\text{min}}
\end{align}$
